# Finitely many isolated points of one fibre at once

Finitely many points of a single fibre of a morphism locally of finite type, each isolated in
that fibre, can be separated into finite opens over one common elementary étale neighbourhood of
the base point.

This material is developed in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.EtaleLocalizationQuasiFinite.FiniteNeighborhood`,
which this file re-exports:
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_elementaryEtaleNeighborhood_finite_opens_of_isolated_fiber_points`
is declared there.

